<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Ishaq Ibrahim I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1283">1283</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Ishaq Ibrahim I was Hafsid sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> from 1279 to 1283, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-zakariya-yahya-i">Abu Zakariya Yahya I</a> and brother of al-Mustansir. With help from the Crown of Aragon he overthrew his nephew Yahya II al-Wathiq. He was driven from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> by the rebel Ibn Abi Umara, who claimed to be a Hafsid prince, and was killed in 1283; his son Abu Zakariya later founded the Hafsid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Béjaïa</a>.</p></div>
